# Semgrep repo-root exclusion for whole-repo self-scans.
#
# The Stage 5 pipeline's working directory is this repo, so the scanner agent
# runs `semgrep-docker scan ... /src` with /src = this repo root. The seed
# fixture under tests/fixtures/secure-scan-demo/ contains intentionally
# vulnerable injection patterns; reporting them as fresh findings on every
# self-scan would block the pipeline with human triage forever. Semgrep
# auto-loads this file from the scan's working directory (=/src via the
# wrapper's --workdir), so these paths are excluded ONLY when scanning this
# repo; real code everywhere else stays scanned.
#
# This file sits OUTSIDE the fixture directory, which is what keeps
# `npm run validate:security:live:e2e` intact: that gate mounts and scans
# tests/fixtures/secure-scan-demo/ itself, where no .semgrepignore exists, so
# each tool's fixture oracle still fires. See README "Security operation
# notes" and tests/fixtures/secure-scan-demo/README.md.

# Deliberately scoped to the only seeded tree: any future REAL file under
# tests/fixtures/ still gets scanned.
tests/fixtures/secure-scan-demo/
